# 📡 MINI RADAR

|--> 1. THE PROBLEM:
Radar is employed for detection of objects and measurement of distance and location.
This project aims to study the way in which an object can be detected at varying distances and area scanning with the help of rotation of sensors.

|--> 2. Solution:
Arduino-based miniature radar device was made that uses ultrasonic sensor along with servo motor.
The ultrasonic sensor is used for detecting distances to various objects and the servo motor moves it at various angles.
The information regarding angle and distance measurements is then sent by Arduino via Serial Monitor.

|--> 3. Why Did We Make It?
The project is a practical construction exercise done in workshops.
Students did not study sensors, servo motors, and Arduino programming in isolation; they integrated the three concepts in one working project.
During the construction of the project, students:
- Studied how ultrasonic sensors determine distance.
- Studied how servo motors control angular displacement.
- Studied Arduino programming.
- Studied how to read data from sensors.
- Dealt with circuit wiring.
- Studied the interaction between sensors and actuators.
- Constructed a simple scanner system.

|--> 4. Workshop Process
The whole procedure was conducted gradually in the workshop.
01 — Learning about the Ultrasonic Sensor
Students were taught about how the HC-SR04 sensor detects the distance between the sensor and the object.
02 — The Concept of the Servo Motor
Servo motor was introduced as an actuator that could turn the sensor at different angles.
03 — Building the Circuit
The Arduino, ultrasonic sensor and servo motor were connected by the students.
04 — Testing the Sensor
Ultrasonic sensor was tested separately for receiving accurate distance measurements.
05 — Controlling the Servo
Servo motor was programmed to turn at different angles.
06 — Integrating the System
Both ultrasonic sensor and servo motor were combined together into a scanning system.

|--> 5. How It Works
The servo motor turns the ultrasonic sensor to different angles.
The HC-SR04 detects the distance from the closest object at each angle.
The data for both the angle and distance is sent via the Serial Monitor by the Arduino.
This gives us a very basic example of:
||--> Sense → Process → Act
Sense:
The ultrasonic sensor senses the distance.
Process:
The Arduino processes the sensor data.
Act:
The servo motor alters the angle of the sensor.

